const contents = [{"label": "What are the alternatives to hiring a marketing agency?", "id": "what-are-the-alternatives-to-hiring-a-marketing-agency"}, {"label": "When is a freelancer the right choice?", "id": "when-is-a-freelancer-the-right-choice"}, {"label": "When does an in-house marketing hire make sense?", "id": "when-does-an-in-house-marketing-hire-make-sense"}, {"label": "Can a small business do its own marketing with AI tools?", "id": "can-a-small-business-do-its-own-marketing-with-ai-tools"}, {"label": "What is an AI marketing team, and how is it different from an agency?", "id": "what-is-an-ai-marketing-team-and-how-is-it-different-from-an-agency"}, {"label": "How much does each option cost?", "id": "how-much-does-each-option-cost"}, {"label": "How do I choose the right option?", "id": "how-do-i-choose-the-right-option"}, {"label": "When is a traditional agency still the better choice?", "id": "when-is-a-traditional-agency-still-the-better-choice"}, {"label": "FAQ", "id": "faq"}, {"label": "Sources and limits", "id": "sources-and-limits"}, {"label": "See what Markethink would do for you", "id": "see-what-markethink-would-do-for-you"}];
const bodyHtml = "<p>None of these is right for everyone. Below is an honest comparison, with costs only where a public source exists.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-are-the-alternatives-to-hiring-a-marketing-agency\">What are the alternatives to hiring a marketing agency?</h2>\n<p>There are four realistic alternatives: hire a freelancer for a specific job, hire an employee to own marketing in-house, do it yourself with AI tools, or use an AI marketing team where AI does the work and marketers review it. Many small businesses combine two of these.</p>\n<div class=\"table-scroll table-scroll--overview\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Comparison table\" tabindex=\"0\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Option</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Who does the work</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Who checks it</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Best for</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Main risk</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Typical cost</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Traditional agency</td>\n<td>Agency staff</td>\n<td>Agency account team</td>\n<td>Bigger budgets, brand campaigns, paid media at scale</td>\n<td>Cost; small accounts can get less attention</td>\n<td>$5,000 to $50,000 per month, ad spend separate (Clutch)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Freelancer</td>\n<td>One specialist</td>\n<td>You</td>\n<td>One clear job: a website, a logo, an ad campaign</td>\n<td>Gaps when they are busy or leave; you manage them</td>\n<td>Varies by person and job; no reliable public figure</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>In-house hire</td>\n<td>Your employee</td>\n<td>You or a manager</td>\n<td>Steady, full-time work close to sales and product</td>\n<td>Cost, hiring time, one person can't cover every skill</td>\n<td>Salary plus benefits (BLS figures below)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DIY with AI tools</td>\n<td>You</td>\n<td>You</td>\n<td>Owners with time, writing skill and patience</td>\n<td>The work stops when you get busy</td>\n<td>Tool subscriptions vary; the real cost is your time</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AI marketing team (Markethink)</td>\n<td>A named AI marketing employee</td>\n<td>Expert marketers, then you</td>\n<td>Weekly work across several channels without a hire</td>\n<td>Not built for big brand campaigns or video production</td>\n<td>From $1,000/month</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h2 id=\"when-is-a-freelancer-the-right-choice\">When is a freelancer the right choice?</h2>\n<p>A freelancer is the right choice when you have one well-defined job with a clear end, like a new website, a logo, a video or a one-off ad campaign, and you have time to brief them and check the work. Freelancers can be excellent specialists; the trade-off is that one person sets the pace.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Pros:</strong> you pick the exact skill; you pay for the job, not a retainer; direct contact with the person doing the work.</li>\n<li><strong>Cons:</strong> work pauses when they are busy, on holiday or move on; you are the reviewer; covering social, email and SEO usually means several freelancers.</li>\n<li><strong>Who it fits:</strong> owners with a single project, or a business that already has someone in-house to manage outside help. Fractional marketers (part-time senior marketers) are a variation that adds strategy, not usually day-to-day production.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Compare a freelancer with Markethink in detail: <a href=\"/compare/markethink-vs-freelancer/\">Markethink vs a freelance marketer</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"when-does-an-in-house-marketing-hire-make-sense\">When does an in-house marketing hire make sense?</h2>\n<p>An in-house hire makes sense when you have enough steady work for a full-time person and you want marketing decisions made close to sales and the owner. It is the most expensive option for a small business, and one person rarely has every skill, from design to SEO to email.</p>\n<p>The U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics puts the median annual wage at $78,760 for market research analysts (the BLS group that includes marketing specialists) and $166,790 for marketing managers, both for May 2025. On top of wages, benefits made up 30.0% of private-industry employer compensation in June 2026. Recruiting, training, software and management time add more.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Pros:</strong> full-time focus; knows the business deeply; can coordinate outside help.</li>\n<li><strong>Cons:</strong> cost and hiring time; one person's skills and sick days; turnover resets the work.</li>\n<li><strong>Who it fits:</strong> businesses with a full-time workload and the budget for a salary. We cover this choice in depth in <a href=\"/blog/outsourced-marketing-vs-in-house-small-business/\">outsourced marketing vs in-house</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"can-a-small-business-do-its-own-marketing-with-ai-tools\">Can a small business do its own marketing with AI tools?</h2>\n<p>Yes, if the owner has time every week. AI writing and design tools make drafts fast, but they don't decide what to post, check that it is right, publish it or follow up on replies. The tools are cheap; the owner's time and consistency are the real cost.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Pros:</strong> lowest cash cost; full control; good for learning what works.</li>\n<li><strong>Cons:</strong> the work stops in a busy week; no second pair of eyes; easy to sound generic.</li>\n<li><strong>Who it fits:</strong> very early businesses, and owners who enjoy marketing. Our <a href=\"/blog/how-to-use-ai-for-marketing-small-business/\">guide to using AI for small business marketing</a> shows where to start.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"what-is-an-ai-marketing-team-and-how-is-it-different-from-an-agency\">What is an AI marketing team, and how is it different from an agency?</h2>\n<p>An AI marketing team is a service where AI does the day-to-day marketing work and human marketers check it before it goes out. With Markethink, a named AI marketing employee writes and publishes your posts, pages, emails and reports every week, and expert marketers review every piece. At an agency, staff do the work.</p>\n<p>Markethink is an AI marketing team for small businesses: a named AI marketing employee does the work every week, and expert marketers review it before anything goes out.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Pros:</strong> consistent weekly output across several channels; expert review built in; you approve in the chat you already use; English and Spanish; plans from $1,000/month.</li>\n<li><strong>Cons:</strong> not the right fit for large brand campaigns, TV or video production, or PR; you still give direction and approve public posts.</li>\n<li><strong>Who it fits:</strong> owners who know marketing matters but don't have the time or team for it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>What this looks like in practice: Pambuddha Homes' outreach employee sent 201 personal emails to new prospects and past contacts in about three weeks, and warm replies reached the owner's chat within minutes. Mango Media's employee built a 15-slide proposal and applied about 15 rounds of edits in one afternoon.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-much-does-each-option-cost\">How much does each option cost?</h2>\n<p>Costs are only comparable for the same work over the same period. Public figures: agencies $5,000 to $50,000 per month (Clutch), in-house wages from $78,760 to $166,790 a year before benefits (BLS), Markethink from $1,000 per month. Freelancer and DIY costs vary too much for one fair number.</p>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Comparison table\" tabindex=\"0\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\">Option</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Cost figure</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Source</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Digital marketing agency</td>\n<td>$5,000 to $50,000 per month; ads budgeted separately</td>\n<td>Clutch, Digital Marketing Agency Pricing Guide 2026, updated 21 Sep 2026</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>In-house hire</td>\n<td>$78,760 (market research analysts) to $166,790 (marketing managers) median annual wage, May 2025; benefits 30.0% of private-industry compensation, June 2026</td>\n<td>BLS Occupational Outlook Handbook; BLS Employer Costs for Employee Compensation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Freelancer</td>\n<td>Not given: rates vary by person, skill and scope</td>\n<td>Get two or three quotes for the same job</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DIY with AI tools</td>\n<td>Not given: subscription prices change often</td>\n<td>Count your own hours at your own hourly value</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Markethink</td>\n<td>From $1,000/month</td>\n<td>Markethink</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p>For every option, add ad spend separately and count the time you spend briefing and reviewing.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-do-i-choose-the-right-option\">How do I choose the right option?</h2>\n<p>Start with the gap, not the vendor. If you have one project, hire a freelancer. If you have a full-time workload and budget, hire someone. If you have time and enjoy it, do it yourself. If you need steady weekly marketing without a hire, use an AI marketing team. If you need big campaigns, use an agency.</p>\n<p>Before you sign with anyone, answer these:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>What exactly needs to go out every week, and on which channels?</li>\n<li>Who checks the work before customers see it?</li>\n<li>What happens when that person is sick, busy or leaves?</li>\n<li>Who owns the accounts, files and website logins?</li>\n<li>What will it cost for the same work over three months, including your own time and ad spend?</li>\n<li>How will you see results each week?</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"when-is-a-traditional-agency-still-the-better-choice\">When is a traditional agency still the better choice?</h2>\n<p>A traditional agency is still the better choice when you need large paid media budgets managed at scale, a full rebrand, video or TV production, PR, or a team in the room for workshops. Those jobs need specialists and senior people for weeks at a time, which is what agency fees pay for.</p>\n<p>Markethink is built for the steady weekly work in between: posts, pages, emails, newsletters and reports. Some businesses use an agency for a launch and Markethink for the weeks after.</p>\n<h2 id=\"faq\">FAQ</h2>\n<details><summary>Is an AI marketing team cheaper than an agency?</summary><p>Usually, for weekly work. Clutch reports agency pricing from $5,000 to $50,000 per month; Markethink plans start at $1,000 per month. Compare the same work over the same period before deciding.</p></details>\n\n<details><summary>Can I combine options?</summary><p>Yes. A common mix is an AI marketing team for weekly posts, emails and pages, plus a freelancer for one-off design or video work.</p></details>\n\n<details><summary>Will AI-written marketing sound generic?</summary><p>It can when nobody checks it. At Markethink, expert marketers review every piece before it reaches you, and your corrections are remembered for the next round.</p></details>\n\n<h2 id=\"sources-and-limits\">Sources and limits</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://clutch.co/agencies/digital-marketing/pricing\">Clutch, Digital Marketing Agency Pricing Guide 2026, by Hannah Hicklen, updated 21 September 2026</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.bls.gov/ooh/business-and-financial/market-research-analysts.htm\">U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, Occupational Outlook Handbook, Market Research Analysts (May 2025 wages)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.bls.gov/ooh/management/advertising-promotions-and-marketing-managers.htm\">U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, Occupational Outlook Handbook, Advertising, Promotions, and Marketing Managers (May 2025 wages)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ecec.nr0.htm\">U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, Employer Costs for Employee Compensation, June 2026</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>National medians and agency-wide ranges are not quotes for your business. The comparison framework is Markethink's own analysis. Markethink's examples come from our own client work; we don't promise the same results for every business.</p>\n<h2 id=\"see-what-markethink-would-do-for-you\">See what Markethink would do for you</h2>\n<p>Tell us where marketing is stuck and we'll tell you honestly which option fits, even if it isn't us. <a href=\"/schedule-a-walkthrough/\">Request a walkthrough</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>About the author:</strong> Santiago Sosa founded Markethink in 2026 in Miami. He has led All Digital Media since 2004 and was Marketing Director at a law office from 2010 to 2017. <a href=\"/authors/santiago-sosa/\">More about Santiago</a></p>";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} image="/images/hero-image.png" type="article" includeSiteEntities={true}>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(pageSchema)} />
  <Navbar />
  <main class="article-page">
    <article>
      <header class="article-hero">
        <div class="container article-hero-copy">
          <h1>Alternatives to a marketing agency for a small business</h1>
          <p class="article-meta">By Santiago Sosa, Founder · Updated 23 November 2026</p>
          <p class="article-excerpt">The main alternatives to a marketing agency are a freelancer, an in-house hire, doing it yourself with AI tools, and an AI marketing team like Markethink. A freelancer suits one clear job, a hire suits steady full-time work, DIY suits owners with spare time, and an AI marketing team suits owners who want reviewed work every week.</p>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="container article-layout">
        <aside class="article-sidebar" aria-label="In this guide">
          <nav class="sidebar-panel" aria-label="Article contents">
            <p class="sidebar-label">In this guide</p>
            <ol>{contents.map((item) => <li><a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a></li>)}</ol>
          </nav>
        </aside>
        <div class="article-content" set:html={bodyHtml} />
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .article-page { background: #F5F5F1; color: #0F1213; }
